<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="2.16.840.1.113883.10.20.22.2.8"/>
    <code code="51848-0" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Evaluation note"/>
    <title>Assessment</title>
    <text><list><item>Memory loss and confusion over about a year, worse in recent months, reported by him and his care partner: repeating stories and questions, losing the thread of conversations, mixing up days, two missed appointments, and once getting lost changing trains on a familiar route; cause to be found: active, confirmed [S]</item><item>Post-traumatic stress disorder, chronic, after two index events (a title fight decades ago after which his opponent died, and a severe assault thirteen years ago): nightmares, unwanted images, avoidance of fight footage, guilt and self-blame, being on guard in crowds, poor sleep; PCL-5 41: active, confirmed [S]</item><item>Personal history of traumatic brain injury: repetitive head impacts over 112 professional bouts, and a severe head injury in an assault thirteen years ago with months in hospital: active, confirmed [S]</item></list></text>

  </section>
</component>

<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="2.16.840.1.113883.10.20.22.2.10" extension="2014-06-09"/>
    <code code="18776-5" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Plan of care note"/>
    <title>Plan of Treatment</title>
    <text><list><item>Cognitive work-up under the Alzheimer&apos;s Association guideline: history from him and his care partner, MoCA, function, depression and PTSD screening, first-tier blood tests (blood count, metabolic panel, B12, TSH), a medicine review for anticholinergic and sedating drugs, a sleep apnea screen, hearing and vision checks, and brain MRI. Guideline: Alzheimer&apos;s Association clinical practice guideline for the Diagnostic Evaluation, Testing, Counseling, and Disclosure of Suspected Alzheimer&apos;s Disease and Related Disorders (DETeCD-ADRD): Executive summary of recommendations for specialty care (2024); Alzheimer&apos;s Association clinical practice guideline for the Diagnostic Evaluation, Testing, Counseling, and Disclosure of Suspected Alzheimer&apos;s Disease and Related Disorders (DETeCD-ADRD): Executive summary of recommendations for primary care (2024); CMID: Clinical Monitoring Intelligence Database, Non-Alzheimer&apos;s dementia and Depression/Bipolar/Mood Disorders monographs (2026) [S]</item><item>Cognitive neurology consultation at the memory clinic to stage the impairment, weigh traumatic brain injury, traumatic encephalopathy syndrome, Alzheimer&apos;s disease, vascular disease and the effects of PTSD and depression, and choose further testing. Guideline: Alzheimer&apos;s Association clinical practice guideline for the Diagnostic Evaluation, Testing, Counseling, and Disclosure of Suspected Alzheimer&apos;s Disease and Related Disorders (DETeCD-ADRD): Executive summary of recommendations for specialty care (2024); National Institute of Neurological Disorders and Stroke Consensus Diagnostic Criteria for Traumatic Encephalopathy Syndrome (2021) [S]</item><item>PTSD treatment by shared decision: cognitive processing therapy with the clinic psychologist, weekly for about twelve sessions, adapted for memory problems; and sertraline 25 mg each morning, raised to 50 mg after four to six weeks if tolerated, with sodium checked two weeks after starting and after the increase; benzodiazepines avoided. Guideline: VA/DoD Clinical Practice Guideline for Management of Posttraumatic Stress Disorder and Acute Stress Disorder (2023); American Geriatrics Society 2023 updated AGS Beers Criteria for potentially inappropriate medication use in older adults (2023) [S]</item><item>Collaborative safety plan with warning signs, coping steps, people to call, the clinic number and the 988 Suicide &amp; Crisis Lifeline; medicines kept by his care partner; PHQ-9 item 9 and safety reviewed at every visit. Guideline: VA/DoD Clinical Practice Guideline for Management of Posttraumatic Stress Disorder and Acute Stress Disorder (2023); VA/DoD Clinical Practice Guideline for Assessment and Management of Patients at Risk for Suicide (2024) [S]</item><item>Falls: STEADI assessment, physical therapy for balance and strength with a home program, and a home safety check. Guideline: CMID: Clinical Monitoring Intelligence Database, Non-Alzheimer&apos;s dementia and Depression/Bipolar/Mood Disorders monographs (2026); STEADI (Stopping Elderly Accidents, Deaths and Injuries): Clinical Resources (2024) [S]</item><item>Measurement-based care: PCL-5 and PHQ-9 at each chronic-care visit during treatment; MoCA yearly or sooner with change; medicine review every visit. Guideline: Alzheimer&apos;s Association clinical practice guideline for the Diagnostic Evaluation, Testing, Counseling, and Disclosure of Suspected Alzheimer&apos;s Disease and Related Disorders (DETeCD-ADRD): Executive summary of recommendations for specialty care (2024); VA/DoD Clinical Practice Guideline for Management of Posttraumatic Stress Disorder and Acute Stress Disorder (2023); CMID: Clinical Monitoring Intelligence Database, Non-Alzheimer&apos;s dementia and Depression/Bipolar/Mood Disorders monographs (2026) [S]</item><item>Advance care planning while he can take part fully: a health care agent, his values and goals of care, at the annual wellness visit. Guideline: Alzheimer&apos;s Association clinical practice guideline for the Diagnostic Evaluation, Testing, Counseling, and Disclosure of Suspected Alzheimer&apos;s Disease and Related Disorders (DETeCD-ADRD): Executive summary of recommendations for specialty care (2024); CMID: Clinical Monitoring Intelligence Database, Non-Alzheimer&apos;s dementia and Depression/Bipolar/Mood Disorders monographs (2026) [S]</item></list></text>

  </section>
